  "articleBody": "Dealing with insurance companies after a car accident can feel like navigating a maze, and honestly, they're not always on your side. Their main goal is often to minimize payouts, so you need to be smart about your interactions.\n\nFirst, always remember that anything you say can be used against your claim. So, when their representative calls, be polite but firm. You only need to provide basic information about the accident – don't go into detail about your injuries or how you feel. It's easy to accidentally say something that could hurt your case later on, like ",
